## DESCRIPTION
## Linear Algebra
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Systems of linear equations)
## DBsection(RREF and rank)
## Date(August 2015)
## Institution(University of Michigan)
## Author(David Sher)
## TitleText1('Linear Algebra with Applications')
## AuthorText1('Otto Bretscher')
## EditionText1('5')
## Section1('1.2')

## New problem for section 1.2

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"PGchoicemacros.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"parserPopUp.pl",
"parserRadioButtons.pl",
);

Context("Numeric");

$radio = RadioButtons(
  [ " No solution", " Exactly one solution"," Infinitely many solutions"],
  " No solution" # correct answer
);

Context("Matrix");

$a=non_zero_random(-7,7,1);
$b=non_zero_random(-7,7,1);
$c=non_zero_random(-3,3,1);
$d=non_zero_random(-3,3,1);
$e=non_zero_random(-3,3,1);
$f=non_zero_random(-3,3,1);
$g=non_zero_random(-3,3,1);

$rk=Compute(3);

$amat=Matrix([[ $g,$a*$g+$e*$g,$b*$g+$c*$e*$g,$d*$e*$g],
[2,2*$a+2*$e,2*$b+2*$c*$e,1+2*$d*$e],
[$f,1+$a*$f+$e*$f,$c+$b*$f+$c*$e*$f,$d+$d*$e*$f]]);
$bmat=Matrix([[1,0,$b-$a*$c,0],[0,1,$c,0],[0,0,0,1]]);

TEXT(beginproblem());
Context()->texStrings;
BEGIN_TEXT

Use SAGE to find the reduced row echelon form of the matrix \(A=$amat\).
$BR
\( \textrm{rref}(A) = \) \{ $bmat->ans_array() \} $BR

$PAR
If \(A\) is the augmented matrix of a system of linear equations, 
how many solutions does the corresponding system have?
$BR
\{ $radio->buttons() \}

END_TEXT
Context()->normalStrings;
# \( \textrm{rank}(A) = \) \{ $rk->ans_rule() \} $BR
ANS( $bmat->cmp() );
# ANS( $rk->cmp() );
ANS( $radio->cmp() );

ENDDOCUMENT();